---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_523",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 523,
  "text": "[[2327.16]] <b>411.  De salute animae curanda [Februar bis Oktober 1685 (?)]</b>\n [[2327.17]] <tab/>[Februar bis Oktober 1685 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[2328.1]] Cum adeo brevis ac misera haec vita sit, anima autem immortalis, monstri simile est\n[[2328.2]] perinde homines vivere, ac si vita in terris aeterna, futura autem nulla esset. Scimus esse\n[[2328.3]] omnipotentem omniaque cognoscentem Deum, apud quem etiam de verbo otioso reddenda\n[[2328.4]] ratio erit, et tamen ita rem gerimus ac si effugere eum aut circumvenire possemus.\n[[2328.5]] Et cum scena sit terra, in qua quisque personam sibi impositam agit, alibi vero majora sint\n[[2328.6]] quibus destinamur, nos tamen verso studio inania tanquam maxime seria tractamus,\n[[2328.7]] cogitatio autem de bonis illis malisque aeternis pene ad scenicam repraesentationem\n[[2328.8]] rediit, nec animos tangit, aut in vitae ratione instituenda vel commutanda quicquam\n[[2328.9]] potest. Quemadmodum enim homines a comoedia aut fabula audita lectave venientes\n[[2328.10]] statim quicquid hoc est, animo ejiciunt, nec magis ejus in re domestica rationem habent,\n[[2328.11]] quam si audivissent nunquam; ita plerique mortales, et maxime illi, qui sibi prae caeteris\n[[2328.12]] sapere videntur atque eminere, lectis Dei gravissimis admonitionibus, audita concione\n[[2328.13]] vehementi ac fulminea peractis Ecclesiae solennibus, aut recitatis domi precum formulis,\n[[2328.14]] mox statim horum omnium obliti pristinum vitae tenorem servant, veluti si a ludicro\n[[2328.15]] aliquo spectaculo ad vera negotia rediissent. </p>\n<p> [[2328.16]] Quam ego caecitatem hominum nostri seculi in cultissimis Europae regionibus\n[[2328.17]] admirans, multo majorem profecto prudentiam in illis seculis ac gentibus agnosco, quibus\n[[2328.18]] barbariem imputamus. Legimus excessu quodam pietatis olim principes de throno descendisse,\n[[2328.19]] aulicos atque in deliciis nutritos in deserta abiisse aut sese in carceres voluntarios\n[[2328.20]] abdidisse, ut unam salutis curam haberent, et Japonenses scimus, perinde ac veteres\n[[2328.21]] martyres, cum hausta semel Christi fide, intelligerent aeternos tandem cruciatus vel\n[[2328.22]] aeterna gaudia quemque manere, gessisse sese, non tanquam haec lecta aut narrata essent,\n[[2328.23]] quae parum afficere solent, sed tanquam hinc coelum apertum illinc horrenda inferni\n[[2328.24]] praecipitia his oculis viderent. Quod profecto sapere est; nos vero aut occulte infideles\n[[2328.25]] sumus, aut si credimus stultissimi, qui tantas spes tanta pericula quae certissima esse\n[[2328.26]] scimus, tam parvi facimus, tantum quia nihil habent, quod sensus corporeos afficiat,\n[[2328.27]] imaginationemque nostram percellat. Cum tamen hoc ipsum sapientis sit ratione potius\n[[2329.1]] quam sensu duci. Scilicet quia nondum audimus mugientem sub pedibus terram, nec\n[[2329.2]] coelestia illa signa videmus, quae rerum commutationem praecedent, securi in diem\n[[2329.3]] vivimus: at barbari quorum fides efficax fuit, surgent contra nos in illa suprema die,\n[[2329.4]] nostramque nobis pudendam ac pene incredibilem negligentiam exprobrabunt. </p>\n<p> [[2329.5]] Porro prima nobis esse debet salutis nostrae cura, proxima alienae, nam quisquis\n[[2329.6]] Christianus est, imo quisquis immortalem in nobis Spiritum Rectoremque universi Deum\n[[2329.7]] credit, eum sibi persuadere oportet, unam animam, etiam quae praepostere judicantibus\n[[2329.8]] vilissima videtur, omnibus mundi bonis pretiosiorem esse. Itaque magni apud Deum fiunt\n[[2329.9]] eorum labores, qui pietatem solidam, qui veram fidem, qui caritatem catholicae unitatis,\n[[2329.10]] quam latissime diffundere suum esse studium volunt. His quanquam ipsa tam praeclari\n[[2329.11]] conatus conscientia magnum satis operae pretium est, immensa tamen praemia statuit\n[[2329.12]] justissimus remunerator, nam qui haustum frigidae aestuanti datum in rationes retulit,\n[[2329.13]] quid illum huic ut ita dicam spirituali Eleemosynae destinasse censemus, ubi sitientes ex\n[[2329.14]] fonte vivo potantur, ubi nudi veste nuptiali induuntur. Neque dubium est beatas illas\n[[2329.15]] animas, quae in hac mundi faece, ubi usque adeo refrixit caritas, nascentis Ecclesiae\n[[2329.16]] ardorem resuscitarunt, et apud gentes feras ac remotas sese martyrio exposuerunt, ut illos\n[[2329.17]] ipsos servarent, a quibus tam crudeliter laniabantur, dulcissimis cogitationibus dolorem\n[[2329.18]] delevisse. </p>\n",
  "number": "411.",
  "title": "De salute animae curanda",
  "date": "[Februar bis Oktober 1685 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:411. De salute animae curanda [Februar bis Oktober 1685 (?)] [Februar bis Oktober 1685 (?)] Cum adeo brevis ac misera haec vita sit, anima autem immortalis, monstri simile est perinde homines vivere, ac si vita in terris aeterna, futura autem nulla esset. Scimus esse omnipotentem omniaque cognoscent...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>